    "As Emily waited for the police to arrive, she realized that she had been carrying the map and flashlight with her. She looked at the map again and saw that there was a small note written in the corner. It said, \"Don't trust anyone in this town.\" Emily's blood ran cold as she thought about the man from the diner and the alleyway. Who else in this town couldn't be trusted? She knew that she had to be careful. ": 1,
    "AUDIO ON": 4,
    "Emily hesitated for a moment but decided to pull over. She rolled down her window and asked the man if he needed any help. He didn't say anything and just stared at her with his dark, soulless eyes. Emily's heart started racing as she realized that something wasn't right. Suddenly, the man lunged towards her, and Emily screamed as she tried to drive away. But it was too late; the man had already grabbed onto her car, and she couldn't shake him off. ": 1,
    "Years later, Emily would still wake up in the middle of the night, covered in sweat, reliving the events of that fateful night. But she also knew that she had done something important. She had helped bring a killer to justice, and she had saved the life of a young girl. And that was something that she could be proud of.": 1,
    "Emily decided to do some investigating of her own. She went online and searched for any information she could find about the disappearances in the town. She found a local newspaper article that mentioned a man named Thomas, who had been missing for over a month. Emily's heart raced as she read the article; the man in the woods had introduced himself as Thomas. ": 1,
    "Emily ran through the woods, branches slapping her in the face, twigs and leaves crunching under her feet. She didn't know where she was going, but she knew she had to keep moving. After what felt like hours, she stumbled upon an old abandoned cabin. It was dark and foreboding, but it was better than being out in the open. ": 1,
    "It was a dark and stormy night as Emily drove down the winding road, her headlights barely illuminating the way ahead. She had taken a wrong turn and was now lost in the middle of nowhere. Suddenly, she saw a figure in the distance, a shadowy figure standing by the side of the road. Emily slowed down, wondering if she should stop and offer help. As she got closer, she realized it was a man, and he was beckoning her to come closer. ": 1,
    "Emily ran until she was out of breath, not stopping until she reached the outskirts of the town. She found a payphone and called the police, telling them everything that had happened to her that night. They promised to send a car to pick her up and take her to the station. ": 1,
