    "After what felt like an eternity, Emily saw the lights of a small town in the distance. She smiled; she had made it. She drove into town and parked the car outside a diner. She went inside and ordered a cup of coffee, trying to warm up her cold and shaking body. ": 1,
    "As Emily walked, she heard strange noises coming from the woods around her. She didn't know what they were, but they sounded like animals. Emily tried to walk faster, but her feet were sore, and her body was exhausted. She didn't know how much longer she could go on. ": 1,
    "Emily's car spun out of control and crashed into a tree. She was dazed and disoriented, trying to make sense of what had just happened. As she looked out of the window, she saw the man walking towards her, his eyes still fixed on her. Emily tried to move, but her seatbelt was jammed, and she couldn't escape. The man reached the car and started pounding on the window, trying to break it open. ": 1,
    "Emily tried to fight back, but the man was too strong. He dragged her deeper into the woods, his grip on her hair unrelenting. She could hear his ragged breathing, feel his hot breath on the back of her neck. Emily knew that she was in grave danger, and she had to find a way to escape before it was too late. ": 1,
    "Emily hesitated for a moment, wondering if she should get in the car. It could be a trap, or it could be someone who wanted to help her. She decided to take the risk and got in the car. It was warm inside, and the seats were comfortable. Emily breathed a sigh of relief, happy to be out of the rain and away from the dangers of the woods. ": 1,
    "As Emily sat in the car, she noticed a map and a flashlight on the passenger seat. She picked them up and examined them. The map showed the way to the nearest town, and the flashlight was fully charged. Emily felt a glimmer of hope; maybe she could find her way back to civilization after all. ": 1
